.TH SDeviceInfo 2type 2026-08-14 "Linux"

.SH NAME
SDeviceInfo \- expansion module representation of piControl driver

.SH LIBRARY
piControl device driver ioctl interface

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B "#include <piControl.h>"
.sp
.B typedef struct SDeviceInfoStr {
.BR "    __u8   i8uAddress;" "        /* Address of module in current configuration */"
.BR "    __u8   pad[3];" "            /* padding for alignment */"
.BR "    __u32  i32uSerialnumber;" "  /* serial number of module */"
.BR "    __u16  i16uModuleType;" "    /* type identifier of module */"
.BR "    __u16  i16uHW_Revision;" "   /* hardware revision */"
.BR "    __u16  i16uSW_Major;" "      /* major firmware version */"
.BR "    __u16  i16uSW_Minor;" "      /* minor firmware version */"
.BR "    __u32  i32uSVN_Revision;" "  /* SVN revision of firmware */"
.BR "    __u16  i16uInputLength;" "   /* length in bytes of all input values together */"
.BR "    __u16  i16uOutputLength;" "  /* length in bytes of all output values together */"
.BR "    __u16  i16uConfigLength;" "  /* length in bytes of all config values together */"
.BR "    __u16  i16uBaseOffset;" "    /* offset in process image */"
.BR "    __u16  i16uInputOffset;" "   /* offset in process image of first input byte */"
.BR "    __u16  i16uOutputOffset;" "  /* offset in process image of first output byte */"
.BR "    __u16  i16uConfigOffset;" "  /* offset in process image of first config byte */"
.BR "    __u16  i16uFirstEntry;" "    /* index of entry */"
.BR "    __u16  i16uEntries;" "       /* number of entries in process image */"
.BR "    __u8   i8uModuleState;" "    /* fieldbus state of piGate Module */"
.BR "    __u8   i8uActive;" "         /* 0 if module is not present and no data is available */"
.BR "    __u16  i16uFeatures;" "      /* feature flags */"
.BR "    __u8   i8uReserve[30];" "    /* reserved space for future extensions */"
.B } SDeviceInfo;
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION
Contains information about an expansion module, as represented by the piControl
driver.

The fields are as follows:

.TP
.I i8uAddress
This field contains the address of the expansion module on the piBridge bus.
.TP
.I pad
This field is padding and must be zeroed.
.TP
.I i32uSerialnumber
This field contains the serial number of the expansion module.
.TP
.I i16uModuleType
This field identifies the type of the expansion module.
.TP
.I i16uHW_Revision
This field contains the hardware revision of the expansion module.
.TP
.I i16uSW_Major
This field contains the major number of the firmware version.
.TP
.I i16uSW_Minor
This field contains the minor number of the firmware version.
.TP
.I i32uSVN_Revision
This field contains the SVN revision of the firmware.
.TP
.I i16uInputLength
This field contains the length in bytes of all input values.
.TP
.I i16uOutputLength
This field contains the length in bytes of all output values.
.TP
.I i16uConfigLength
This field contains the length in bytes of all config values.
.TP
.I i16uBaseOffset
This field contains the offset in bytes in the process image.
.TP
.I i16uInputOffset
This field contains the offset in bytes of the first input value.
.TP
.I i16uOutputOffset
This field contains the offset in bytes of the first output value.
.TP
.I i16uConfigOffset
This field contains the offset in bytes of the first configuration value.
.TP
.I i16uFirstEntry
This field contains the index of the first entry in the process image.
.TP
.I i16uEntries
This field contains the number of entries in the process image.
.TP
.I i8uModuleState
This field contains the state of a gateway expansion module.
.TP
.I i8uActive
This field contains the active state of the expansion module. A
.I 0
means the expansion module is not present, and consequently that no data is
available.
.TP
.I i16uFeatures
This field contains feature flags.
.TP
.I i8uReserve
This field is reserved for future extensions. It must be zeroed.

.P
The following feature flags are defined for the
.I i16uFeatures
field:

.TP
Bit 0
The device supports data exchange using Ethernet.

.TP
Bit 1
The device supports data exchange using RS-485.

.TP
Bit 2-3
The baudrate a device supports.
.B 0
is a baudrate of 115200,
.B 1
is a baudrate of 500000,
.B 2
is a baudrate of 1000000, and
.B 3
is a baudrate of 1500000.

.TP
Bit 4
The device supports CRC-16 as the checksum in the IO protocol instead of the
XOR-based checksum.

.SH SEE ALSO

.BR ioctl (2),
.BR KB_GET_DEVICE_INFO (2),
.BR KB_GET_DEVICE_INFO_LIST (2)
